Notes:
- 'Empty RSS' is the footprint right after new(capacity), before any inserts.
  Fixed-capacity structures that pre-allocate and zero their storage (PulseMap,
  quick_cache) will show most of their footprint here already.
- 'Filled RSS' is after inserting up to 100% capacity — the honest steady-state
  number, since Linux won't count untouched allocated pages toward RSS.
- 'Bytes/entry' = filled RSS / capacity. Compare this directly against README
  claims like '14B packed slot vs 48B LRU pointers' — this is real, not theoretical.
